"The oldest known writing comes from the city of Uruk, about 3350 to 3000 BCE. A scribe pressed the end of a cut reed into wet clay, and the tablet hardened as it dried in the hot, dry air. Most of these early tablets are accounts: grain, animals, workers, and the food paid to them. A smaller number are lists of words, probably used to train scribes. Writing here began as a tool for keeping track of things.": "25470494bd30",
